            <ArticleTitle>Endoscopic esophageal self-expanding stent implantation WallFlex™ (Boston Scientific) in the management of a gastrocutaneous fistula, as a complication of sleeve bariatric gastrectomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>320-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1515/pjs-2015-0062</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">/j/pjs.2015.87.issue-6/pjs-2015-0062/pjs-2015-0062.xml</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The study presented a case of a gastrocutaneous fistula, as a result of bariatric sleeve gastrectomy. The discussion considered the main pathogenesis, etiology, diagnostics and endoscopic treatment using the implantation of covered esophageal stents. Special attention was placed upon the multifactorial origin of this life-threatening clinical condition, typical for bariatric surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
